WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.620
Morning, in a young offenders' unit.

2
00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:06.240
A teenager makes their bed
and is handed a plastic token.

3
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.900
Another goes to class.

4
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.100
Another token, into the jar.

5
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.760
At the end of the week, the tokens are
swapped for a snack and extra gym time.

6
00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.480
Isn't that just bribery?

7
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.800
Or is it psychology that works?

8
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.150
In this mission, you'll see
how a token economy works:

9
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.350
target behaviours, tokens, and rewards.

10
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.560
You'll find out why a token,
worth nothing on its own,

11
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.880
is called a secondary reinforcer.

12
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:35.190
And you'll compare it with a very
different treatment: anger management.

13
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:40.670
Your mission: decide whether token economies
are bribery or psychology that works.
